               <exData contentType="text/html">
                  <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">1) Enter the intermittent worker's information, or verify that the auto lookup information is correct.</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">2) Enter "HOURS WORKED," not starting and ending times.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="color:#de0000">Enter time as Hours : Minutes.</span></p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">Use the Tab Key to move from one cell to the next when entering hours and minutes. For example, 5 and</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">1/2 hours should be entered as<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="color:#de0000">5:30</span>, not 5.5. You also may click in a cell with your mouse</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">to make an entry. Shift-Tab will take you back to the previous cell. If the person worked 5 hours, you can</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">enter 5 for hours ; you would need to enter "00" for minutes. Similarly, if the person worked for 45 minutes, you can enter 45 for minutes; you would need to enter "00" for hours.</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">3) Enter hours for one pay period only on a single calendar timesheet. Do not add hours worked during</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">the previous or next pay period. The totals for the pay period will be calculated for you.</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">4) You may use tabs to move from one cell to the next cell. If you don't want to tab through sick</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">and vacation hours, you can select the next work day with your mouse. You may move directly to any cell</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">with your mouse.</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">5) Add Signature under Signature and<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="letter-spacing:0em">Acknowledgment</span> section.</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in">5) Submit the form after entering the data.</p><p style="font-size:12pt;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p></body>
               </exData>
